      "publish_date": null,
      "excerpts": [
        "This document describes how OpenCode stores session data internally, based on analysis of the opencode source.\nStorage layers\nOpenCode uses two complementary storage systems:\n1. SQLite database (~/.opencode/data.db)\nPrimary persistence for all structured session data. Uses Drizzle ORM with Effect-TS on the application side.\nTables:\n* Table | Purpose\n* project | Project metadata (id, name, worktree path)\n* session | Session metadata, config, token/cost stats\n* message | V1 message storage (role + content JSON)\n* part | V1 message parts (text, tool-call, file, reasoning)\n* session_message | V2 messages (current format, sequenced)\n* session_input | User prompts/inputs linked to messages\n* todo | Task items bound to sessions\n* session_context_epoch | Context compaction state\n2. Git-based snapshots (~/.opencode/snapshot/)\nFile-level undo/revert system. Each project gets a separate git repository (bare-style) at:\n~/.opencode/snapshot/{project_id}/{worktree_hash}/\nEach snapshot is a git commit tracking the working tree state at that moment. Allows reverting file changes made during a session.\nSession lifecycle\n1. Creation — new row in session table, linked to a project\n2. Messages — stored in both V1 (message + part) and V2 (session_message) formats\n3. Inputs — user prompts tracked in session_input with admission/promotion sequencing\n4. Snapshots — file state captured in the git snapshot repo before tool executions\n5.\nMessage formats\nV1 (legacy, still populated)\n* message table: {id, session_id, data: {role, content, ...}}\n* part table: {id, message_id, session_id, data: {type, ...}}\n  Part types include: text, reasoning, tool-call, tool-result, file, error\nV2 (current primary)\nproject (1) ─── (*) session\nsession (1) ─── (*) message ─── (*) part\nsession (1) ─── (*) session_message\nsession (1) ─── (*) session_input\nsession (1) ─── (*) todo\nsession (1) ─── (0..1) session_context_epoch\nsession (0..1) ─── (parent) session  [forking]\nData locations summary\n* Data | Location\n* Session metadata | data.db → session table\n* Messages (V1) | data.db → message + part tables\n* Messages (V2) | data.db → session_message table\n* User inputs | data.db → session_input table\n* Todos | data.db → todo table\n* Compaction state | data.db → session_context_epoch table\n* File snapshots | ~/.opencode/snapshot/{project}/{hash}/ (git)\n* Plans | {worktree}/.opencode/plans/ or ~/.opencode/plans/\nDatabase path resolution\nThe database file name and location are resolved at startup via packages/core/src/database/database.ts:\nPriority 1: OPENCODE_DB environment variable\n- absolute path  → use directly\n- relative name  → join with $XDG_DATA_HOME/opencode/\n- \":memory:\"     → in-memory SQLite\nPriority 2: Channel-based naming\n* Variable | Effect\n* OPENCODE_DB | Override database file path (absolute or relative to data dir)\n* XDG_DATA_HOME | Override base data directory (default: ~/.local/share)\n* OPENCODE_DISABLE_CHANNEL_DB | Set to 1 to always use opencode.db regardless of channel\nExamples"
