        "markporter/opencode_tutorial — docs/04-extending-opencode/04-plugins/creating-plugins.md\nLearn to build plugins that extend OpenCode and Oh My OpenCode functionality.\n🎯 Understanding OpenCode Plugins\nImportant: OpenCode's plugin system is limited compared to other tools. For most use cases, you should use:\n🛠️ Prerequisites\nBefore building a plugin:\n* JavaScript/TypeScript knowledge - Plugins use Node.js\n* npm or Bun - Package management\n* OpenCode installed - For testing\n* Familiarity with MCPs - Consider this instead\n📁 Plugin Structure\nMinimal Plugin\nEvery plugin needs metadata:\n{\n\"name\": \"@myorg/opencode-my-plugin\",\n\"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n\"description\": \"My custom OpenCode plugin\",\n\"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n\"author\": \"Your Name\",\n\"license\": \"MIT\",\n\"keywords\": [\"opencode\", \"plugin\"],\n\"files\": [\"dist\", \"README.md\"],\n\"scripts\": {\n\"build\": \"tsc\",\n\"dev\": \"tsc --watch\"\n},\n\"devDependencies\": {\n🚀 Creating Your First Plugin\nStep 1: Initialize Project\nmkdir my-opencode-plugin\ncd my-opencode-plugin\nnpm init -y\nnpm install --save-dev typescript @types/node\nStep 2: Create TypeScript Config\nFile: tsconfig.json\n{\n\"compilerOptions\": {\n\"target\": \"ES2020\",\n\"module\": \"commonjs\",\n\"lib\": [\"ES2020\"],\n\"outDir\": \"./dist\",\n\"rootDir\": \"./src\",\n\"strict\": true,\n\"esModuleInterop\": true,\n\"skipLibCheck\": true,\n\"forceConsistentCasingInFileNames\": true\n},\n\"include\": [\"src\"],\n\"exclude\": [\"node_modules\"]\n}\nStep 3: Write Basic Plugin\nFile: src/index.ts\nexport default class MyPlugin {\nname = 'my-plugin';\nversion = '1.0.0';\nasync initialize(): Promise<void> {\nconsole.log('MyPlugin initialized');\n}\nasync destroy(): Promise<void> {\nconsole.log('MyPlugin destroyed');\n}\n}\nStep 4: Build and Test\nnpm run build\nCreate .opencode directory if it doesn't exist\nmkdir -p ~/.opencode/plugins\nCopy plugin for testing\ncp -r . ~/.opencode/plugins/my-plugin\n💡 Example 1: Configuration Plugin\nScenario: Load custom settings on startup\nFile: src/index.ts\ninterface PluginConfig {\nautoSaveInterval: number;\ndefaultModel: string;\ntheme: 'dark' | 'light';\n}\nCopy plugin for testing\n}\nasync destroy(): Promise<void> {\nconsole.log('Slack notifications disabled');\n}\n}\n🎯 Installation & Usage\nInstall a Published Plugin\nnpm install @myorg/opencode-plugin\nUse from Local Directory\nOption 1: Copy to plugins directory\ncp -r my-plugin ~/.opencode/plugins/\nOption 2: Link for development\ncd my-plugin && npm link\ncd ~/.opencode/plugins && npm link my-plugin\nEnable in Configuration\nFile: ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json or .opencode/oh-my"
